English translation of the original Japanese commit message:

fix(stream): preserve discontinuity on the first resumed chunk

In crates/flexaudio/src/stream.rs, update resume_generation and clear
paused under the delivery lock. Each tap checks the generation under
that same lock when enqueueing, so its first resumed chunk receives
DISCONTINUITY rather than a later chunk winning the race. Primary and
secondary taps track generations independently; chunks discarded while
paused do not advance their observed generation. Sequence numbers stay
continuous, with no silence inserted for pauses. Keep
discontinuity_pending for source switching and recovery. Add a 300-round
test for both taps. The message notes that the old code also passed: the
test checks behavior but did not reproduce the race. Shared locking
closes the faulty interleaving.
